      ":question/worked-solution": "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $14$ is a positive whole number, so it belongs to $N.$ We can write\n\n$$\n14\\in N\n$$\n\n- Every natural number is an integer, rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}14\\in Z\\qquad 14\\in Q \\\\ 14\\in R\\qquad 14\\in C\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $N, Z, Q, R, C$."
